{"type":"tool_call_update","toolCallId":"call-400a236d-696c-45b0-959b-0a6bcfd3ff02-5","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"1→# Vengeons framework vs kr8tiv.io (Nov 6 2026)\nSource: Paul Vengeons, \"The Google Algorithm Explained, In Depth…\" https://x.com/VengeonsP/status/2118661285868863578\nNo Search Console export on disk — every query/CTR claim below needs Matt's GSC paste.\n\n## 1. Scouts (crawl/render/index)\nGood: Astro static = answers in raw HTML; service pages carry title/H1 with query words (\"Storefront & Sign Design in Edmonton\"); HowTo schema; robots.txt, llms.txt, sitemap exist; type is live HTML over video plates (not baked in).\nGaps: verify video/JS hero doesn't push the H1+answer below hydration; first 100 words must contain the query + Edmonton; sitemap must exclude noindex drafts, /menu-lab, /build-notes; internal links into new service pages are thin (mostly nav).\n\n## 2. Judge (siteAuthority, focus/siteRadius, contentEffort)\n10→Good: tight focus = \"Edmonton creative studio: web, brand, print/signage\". Real pricing (web from $1,200, landing $600, sign concept ~$500 + variable PM) is first-hand material.\nGaps: little proof a human did it — no process photos, real project notes, fabricator workflow detail, author bylines on Field notes. Home (strongest page) should link down to each service with descriptive anchors.\n\n## 3. NavBoost (click, stay, return)\nGaps: titles are descriptive but not click-winning; first screen should answer \"what, price, Edmonton, next step\" before scroll; nothing yet drives brand returns (Field notes series, newsletter, \"KR8TIV\" branded searches).\n\n## 4. Bouncer (demotion)\nRisks for us: (a) spinning one page per collateral item × city = thin scaled pages; (b) FAR queries (generic \"logo ideas\", \"what is SEO\") dilute siteRadius; (c) keyword-stuffed anchors; (d) publishing 5 drafts without first-hand effort.\nRule: one strong collateral hub + a few deep children only where there is real distinct demand and real material.\n"}}],"rawOutput":{"type":"ReadFile","FileContent":{"content":"1→# Vengeons framework vs kr8tiv.io (Nov 6 2026)\nSource: Paul Vengeons, \"The Google Algorithm Explained, In Depth…\" https://x.com/VengeonsP/status/2118661285868863578\nNo Search Console export on disk — every query/CTR claim below needs Matt's GSC paste.\n\n## 1. Scouts (crawl/render/index)\nGood: Astro static = answers in raw HTML; service pages carry title/H1 with query words (\"Storefront & Sign Design in Edmonton\"); HowTo schema; robots.txt, llms.txt, sitemap exist; type is live HTML over video plates (not baked in).\nGaps: verify video/JS hero doesn't push the H1+answer below hydration; first 100 words must contain the query + Edmonton; sitemap must exclude noindex drafts, /menu-lab, /build-notes; internal links into new service pages are thin (mostly nav).\n\n## 2. Judge (siteAuthority, focus/siteRadius, contentEffort)\n10→Good: tight focus = \"Edmonton creative studio: web, brand, print/signage\". Real pricing (web from $1,200, landing $600, sign concept ~$500 + variable PM) is first-hand material.\nGaps: little proof a human did it — no process photos, real project notes, fabricator workflow detail, author bylines on Field notes. Home (strongest page) should link down to each service with descriptive anchors.\n\n## 3. NavBoost (click, stay, return)\nGaps: titles are descriptive but not click-winning; first screen should answer \"what, price, Edmonton, next step\" before scroll; nothing yet drives brand returns (Field notes series, newsletter, \"KR8TIV\" branded searches).\n\n## 4. Bouncer (demotion)\nRisks for us: (a) spinning one page per collateral item × city = thin scaled pages; (b) FAR queries (generic \"logo ideas\", \"what is SEO\") dilute siteRadius; (c) keyword-stuffed anchors; (d) publishing 5 drafts without first-hand effort.\nRule: one strong collateral hub + a few deep children only where there is real distinct demand and real material.\n","content_concise":"1→# Vengeons framework vs kr8tiv.io (Nov 6 2026)\nSource: Paul Vengeons, \"The Google Algorithm Explained, In Depth…\" https://x.com/VengeonsP/status/2118661285868863578\nNo Search Console export on disk — every query/CTR claim below needs Matt's GSC paste.\n\n## 1. Scouts (crawl/render/index)\nGood: Astro static = answers in raw HTML; service pages carry title/H1 with query words (\"Storefront & Sign Design in Edmonton\"); HowTo schema; robots.txt, llms.txt, sitemap exist; type is live HTML over video plates (not baked in).\nGaps: verify video/JS hero doesn't push the H1+answer below hydration; first 100 words must contain the query + Edmonton; sitemap must exclude noindex drafts, /menu-lab, /build-notes; internal links into new service pages are thin (mostly nav).\n\n## 2. Judge (siteAuthority, focus/siteRadius, contentEffort)\n10→Good: tight focus = \"Edmonton creative studio: web, brand, print/signage\". Real pricing (web from $1,200, landing $600, sign concept ~$500 + variable PM) is first-hand material.\nGaps: little proof a human did it — no process photos, real project notes, fabricator workflow detail, author bylines on Field notes. Home (strongest page) should link down to each service with descriptive anchors.\n\n## 3. NavBoost (click, stay, return)\nGaps: titles are descriptive but not click-winning; first screen should answer \"what, price, Edmonton, next step\" before scroll; nothing yet drives brand returns (Field notes series, newsletter, \"KR8TIV\" branded searches).\n\n## 4. Bouncer (demotion)\nRisks for us: (a) spinning one page per collateral item × city = thin scaled pages; (b) FAR queries (generic \"logo ideas\", \"what is SEO\") dilute siteRadius; (c) keyword-stuffed anchors; (d) publishing 5 drafts without first-hand effort.\nRule: one strong collateral hub + a few deep children only where there is real distinct demand and real material.\n","absolute_path":"/workspace/kio-seo-imagine/build-plan-seo-vengeons/docs/ALIGNMENT.md","offset":null,"raw_output":"# Vengeons framework vs kr8tiv.io (Nov 6 2026)\nSource: Paul Vengeons, \"The Google Algorithm Explained, In Depth…\" https://x.com/VengeonsP/status/2118661285868863578\nNo Search Console export on disk — every query/CTR claim below needs Matt's GSC paste.\n\n## 1. Scouts (crawl/render/index)\nGood: Astro static = answers in raw HTML; service pages carry title/H1 with query words (\"Storefront & Sign Design in Edmonton\"); HowTo schema; robots.txt, llms.txt, sitemap exist; type is live HTML over video plates (not baked in).\nGaps: verify video/JS hero doesn't push the H1+answer below hydration; first 100 words must contain the query + Edmonton; sitemap must exclude noindex drafts, /menu-lab, /build-notes; internal links into new service pages are thin (mostly nav).\n\n## 2. Judge (siteAuthority, focus/siteRadius, contentEffort)\nGood: tight focus = \"Edmonton creative studio: web, brand, print/signage\". Real pricing (web from $1,200, landing $600, sign concept ~$500 + variable PM) is first-hand material.\nGaps: little proof a human did it — no process photos, real project notes, fabricator workflow detail, author bylines on Field notes. Home (strongest page) should link down to each service with descriptive anchors.\n\n## 3. NavBoost (click, stay, return)\nGaps: titles are descriptive but not click-winning; first screen should answer \"what, price, Edmonton, next step\" before scroll; nothing yet drives brand returns (Field notes series, newsletter, \"KR8TIV\" branded searches).\n\n## 4. Bouncer (demotion)\nRisks for us: (a) spinning one page per collateral item × city = thin scaled pages; (b) FAR queries (generic \"logo ideas\", \"what is SEO\") dilute siteRadius; (c) keyword-stuffed anchors; (d) publishing 5 drafts without first-hand effort.\nRule: one strong collateral hub + a few deep children only where there is real distinct demand and real material.\n","total_lines":18}},"locations":[]}
