uy another buzzword. From Edmonton, useful wherever you’re building. Draft · in review When does a custom website pay off for an Alberta business? A decision-and-brief worksheet for website economics, page planning, immersive design, accessibility, search, and migration. KR8TIV Agency · drafted November 6, 2026 Draft · in review How to design an amazing storefront sign in Edmonton A\n\\n=== /blog/local-advertising-edmonton-alberta/ ===\ntitle: Local advertising in Edmonton: a useful test | KR8TIV\ndesc: Plan local ads for Edmonton and Alberta with honest budgets, better targeting, useful video, and qualified-lead tracking. Build a test before spending more.\ncanon: https://kr8tiv.io/blog/local-advertising-edmonton-alberta/\nrobots: noindex,nofollow\nh1: [\"How to run local advertising that brings better enquiries in Edmonton\"]\nwords: \u001b[33m1748\u001b[39m video: \u001b[33m0\u001b[39m scripts: \u001b[33m10\u001b[39m\nflags: ok\nout: /, /work/, /process/, /blog/, /start/, /terms/, /services/web-design-edmonton/, /services/branding/, /services/print-signage-design/\nin: /blog/\nunres: \n100: 侍 KR8TIV / · 08 HOME DOCTRINE WHY WORK PROCESS NOTES START TERMS 780-915-5471 ⌘ K ← Field notes · Draft for Matt’s review — not yet published · drafted November 6, 2026 · KR8TIV Agency How to run local advertising that brings better enquiries in Edmonton Local advertising works best when the targeting, message, landing page, and follow-up all describe the same service. Choose a specific buying situation, reach the people you can genuinely serve, and judge results by qualified enquiries and sales rather than cheap clicks. A small Edmonton business does not need a national media plan to\n\\n=== /blog/marketing-campaign-edmonton/ ===\ntitle: How to build a marketing campaign in Edmonton | KR8TIV\ndesc: Build an Edmonton marketing campaign around a clear offer, useful creative, and qualified enquiries. Includes a worked example and a first-month plan.\ncanon: https://kr8tiv.io/blog/marketing-campaign-edmonton/\nrobots: noindex,nofollow\nh1: [\"How to build a marketing campaign that brings in customers in Edmonton\"]\nwords: \u001b[33m1804\u001b[39m video: \u001b[33m0\u001b[39m scripts: \u001b[33m10\u001b[39m\nflags: ok\nout: /, /work/, /process/, /blog/, /start/, /terms/, /services/web-design-edmonton/, /services/branding/, /services/print-signage-design/\nin: /blog/\nunres: \n100: 侍 KR8TIV / · 08 HOME DOCTRINE WHY WORK PROCESS NOTES START TERMS 780-915-5471 ⌘ K ← Field notes · Draft for Matt’s review — not yet published · drafted November 6, 2026 · KR8TIV Agency How to build a marketing campaign that brings in customers in Edmonton A useful marketing campaign connects one customer problem to one clear offer, then measures whether the resulting enquiries become profitable work. Start with the job you want to sell, build a page that answers the buyer’s questions, and choose a channel that reaches people who need that job done. At KR8TIV ·\n\\n=== /blog/storefront-sign-design-edmonton/ ===\ntitle: Storefront & sign design in Edmonton: a buyer guide | KR8TIV\ndesc: Plan your Edmonton sign and storefront: concept design, immersive store experiences and project management across Alberta and Canada. Pricing and scope explained.\ncanon: https://kr8tiv.io/blog/storefront-sign-design-edmonton/\nrobots: noindex,nofollow\nh1: [\"How to design an amazing storefront sign in Edmonton\"]\nwords: \u001b[33m2092\u001b[39m video: \u001b[33m0\u001b[39m scripts: \u001b[33m10\u001b[39m\nflags: ok\nout: /, /work/, /process/, /blog/, /start/, /terms/, /services/web-design-edmonton/, /services/branding/, /services/print-signage-design/\nin: /blog/, /services/print-signage-design/\nunres: \n100: 侍 KR8TIV / · 08 HOME DOCTRINE WHY WORK PROCESS NOTES START TERMS 780-915-5471 ⌘ K ← Field notes · Draft for Matt’s review — not yet published · drafted November 6, 2026 · KR8TIV Agency How to design an amazing storefront sign in Edmonton An amazing sign helps the right person recognise your business, understand what you do, and find the entrance. Choose the message and viewing conditions first. Then choose the materials, illumination, and fabrication method that make that message work in the real location. A sign can be beautiful up close and unreadable across the parking lot.\n\\n=== /blog/website-that-earns-its-keep-alberta/ ===\ntitle: When a custom website pays off in Alberta | KR8TIV\ndesc: Decide what your Alberta business website needs before a rebuild. Work through costs, buyer questions, local SEO, accessibility, and a safer launch plan.\ncanon: https://kr8tiv.io/blog/website-that-earns-its-keep-alberta/\nrobots: noindex,nofollow\nh1: [\"When does a custom website pay off for an Alberta business?\"]\nwords: \u001b[33m1740\u001b[39m video: \u001b[33m0\u001b[39m scripts: \u001b[33m10\u001b[39m\nflags: ok\nout: /, /work/, /process/, /blog/, /start/, /terms/, /services/web-design-edmonton/, /services/branding/, /services/print-signage-design/\nin: /blog/\nunres: \n100: 侍 KR8TIV / · 08 HOME DOCTRINE WHY WORK PROCESS NOTES START TERMS 780-915-5471 ⌘ K ← Field notes · Draft for Matt’s review — not yet published · drafted November 6, 2026 · KR8TIV Agency When does a custom website pay off for an Alberta business? A custom website pays off when it solves a specific business problem better than your current site, at a cost the resulting value can support. That problem might be poor enquiries, an unclear service offer, awkward booking, or a buying experience that does not match the quality of your work. Start with that\n\\n=== /build-notes/ ===\ntitle: How we built KR8TIV · Prism\ndesc: Build notes on the KR8TIV Prism hero: WebGL shader refraction, Lenis + GSAP sync, SVG liquid-glass filter, GSAP 3.13 SplitText with ARIA, Astro 5 island architecture.\ncanon: https://kr8tiv.io/build-notes/\nrobots: (absent — default index,follow)\nh1: [\"Build notes: Prism (VIII)\"]\nwords: \u001b[33m1392\u001b[39m video: \u001b[33m0\u001b[39m scripts: \u